    "body": "- Replace newlines in the current cmdline with NULs when opening cmdwin,\n  and do the reverse when putting a cmdwin line back into the cmdline.\n- Escape control characters with Ctrl-V when feeding cmdline.\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-06-30T12:00:32Z",
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "_links": {
                "html": {
                    "href": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40488#discussion_r3495402706"
                },
                "pull_request": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/40488"
                },
                "self": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/comments/3495402706"
                }
            },
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "These mappings are covered by `Test_compl_in_cmdwin()` in test_ins_complete.vim. Without these mappings a `<Tab>` is inserted literally in the buffer, however before this PR the `<Tab>` then expands the completion when returning to cmdline mode, causing the test to pass by accident. Now these mappings are needed for the test to pass.",
            "commit_id": "6a346e8aa653606dd4132639d879545e594b9830",
            "created_at": "2026-06-30T00:12:16Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -92,6 +93,11 @@ function M.open(type, init_line, init_col)\n     vim.bo[buf].filetype = 'vim'\n   end\n \n+  if vim.o.wildchar == ('\\t'):byte() then\n+    vim.keymap.set('i', '<Tab>', '<C-X><C-V>', { buf = buf })\n+    vim.keymap.set('n', '<Tab>', 'a<C-X><C-V>', { buf = buf })\n+  end\n+",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40488#discussion_r3495402706",
